      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "A Deployment's pods are interchangeable: random names, nothing of their own, and any one can stand in for another."
        },
        {
          "text": "That suits our API, which keeps all of its data somewhere else."
        },
        {
          "text": "A database is that somewhere else. It needs a name that stays put, and a disk that belongs to it."
        },
        {
          "text": "That's what a StatefulSet gives you: pods named postgres-0, postgres-1 and so on, each with its own volume."
        },
        {
          "text": "They start in order, one at a time, and a replacement pod gets the same name and the same disk."
        },
        {
          "text": "We'll run a single replica, from a plain StatefulSet and the official image. Replication and backups are a topic of their own, and they stay out of scope.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sts-yaml",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/postgres-statefulset.yaml",
      "range": [
        1,
        24
      ],
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            1,
            13
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            9,
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "lines": [
            14,
            24
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Here's the StatefulSet. At first glance it's a Deployment: a name, one replica, a selector."
        },
        {
          "text": "One new field, serviceName, names the Service that gives each pod its own DNS name. More on that shortly."
        },
        {
          "text": "The pod template runs the official Postgres 17 image, listening on port 5432.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sts-pod",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/postgres-statefulset.yaml",
      "range": [
        25,
        43
      ],
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            25,
            27
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            28,
            30
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "lines": [
            31,
            34
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "lines": [
            41,
            43
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Its user, password and database name come straight from the Secret we made in Episode 3."
        },
        {
          "text": "PGDATA points one folder down, because Postgres wants an empty data directory, and a fresh volume isn't always empty."
        },
        {
          "text": "Its readiness probe runs pg_isready, a small tool that ships with Postgres and asks whether it's taking connections."
        },
        {
          "text": "And the data directory is mounted from a volume called data. So where does that volume come from?",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-yaml",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/postgres-statefulset.yaml",
      "range": [
        41,
        52
      ],
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            44,
            47
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            48,
            48
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "lines": [
            49,
            49
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "lines": [
            50,
            52
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "From volumeClaimTemplates. Instead of naming a volume, the StatefulSet stamps out a claim for each pod."
        },
        {
          "text": "ReadWriteOnce means one node at a time may mount it."
        },
        {
          "text": "The storage class is local-path, which comes built into k3s."
        },
        {
          "text": "And each claim asks for five gigabytes.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "storage",
      "type": "diagram",
      "title": "Where the disk comes from",
      "boxes": [
