          ],
          "tone": {
            "dir": "warn"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": 6,
          "focus": []
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "To start postgres-0, the StatefulSet first makes that pod's claim, data-postgres-0: five gigabytes, please."
        },
        {
          "text": "A claim is only a request. The local-path provisioner sees it, and makes a PersistentVolume to match."
        },
        {
          "text": "That volume is nothing fancy: a folder on one node's own disk."
        },
        {
          "text": "The claim binds to the volume, and the pod mounts the claim."
        },
        {
          "text": "Delete the pod, and the claim and the folder stay. The new postgres-0 mounts the same data."
        },
        {
          "text": "The catch is that the folder sits on one node. The pod can only run there, and losing that node loses the data."
        },
        {
          "text": "On a real on-prem cluster you'd use replicated storage like Longhorn, or keep the database outside the cluster. For learning, local-path is fine.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.5,
          "senses": {
            "use": "verb"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "headless",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/postgres-service.yaml",
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            3,
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            10,
            11
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "lines": [
            1,
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "lines": [
            12,
            17
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The last piece is the Service the StatefulSet named, also called postgres."
        },
        {
          "text": "clusterIP: None makes it headless. There's no shared address in front, because there's nothing to spread traffic across."
        },
        {
          "text": "Instead, DNS hands out each pod's own address, so postgres-0.postgres always means that one pod."
        },
        {
          "text": "That full name is what our ConfigMap has pointed at since Episode 3. It didn't exist yet, so the API kept getting: no such host.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "apply",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl apply -f manifests/base/postgres-service.yaml",
          "output": [
            "service/postgres created"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "kubectl apply -f manifests/base/postgres-statefulset.yaml",
          "output": [
            "statefulset.apps/postgres created"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "command": "kubectl get statefulset,pods -l app.kubernetes.io/name=postgres -n golinks",
          "output": [
            "NAME                        READY   AGE",
            "statefulset.apps/postgres   1/1     38s",
            "",
            "NAME             READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE",
            "pod/postgres-0   1/1     Running   0          38s"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "command": "kubectl describe pvc -n golinks | grep -E '^(Name|Status|Volume|Capacity):'",
          "output": [
            "Name:          data-postgres-0",
            "Status:        Bound",
            "Volume:        pvc-4b1e7c2a-9d3f-4e6b-8a5c-1f2d3e4a5b6c",
            "Capacity:      5Gi"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Apply the Service first, so the name is waiting."
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the StatefulSet."
        },
        {
          "text": "Half a minute later, postgres-0 is running, and ready.",
          "senses": {
            "minute": "time"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "And its claim is bound to a fresh five gigabyte volume.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ready",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl logs postgres-0 -n golinks --tail=2",
          "output": [
            "2026-11-02 14:20:58.221 UTC [64] LOG:  database system was shut down at 2026-11-02 14:20:57 UTC",
            "2026-11-02 14:20:58.229 UTC [1] LOG:  database system is ready to accept connections"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "command": "kubectl get pods -l app.kubernetes.io/name=golinks -n golinks",
          "output": [
            "NAME                       READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE",
            "golinks-7d9c5b6f4d-v8mzq   1/1     Running   0          18m",
            "golinks-7d9c5b6f4d-wq7tn   1/1     Running   0          15m"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 4,
          "command": "kubectl logs deploy/golinks -n golinks --tail=2",
          "output": [
            "Found 2 pods, using pod/golinks-7d9c5b6f4d-v8mzq",
            "{\"time\":\"2026-11-02T14:21:03Z\",\"level\":\"INFO\",\"msg\":\"database connected\"}",
            "{\"time\":\"2026-11-02T14:21:03Z\",\"level\":\"INFO\",\"msg\":\"migrations applied\",\"count\":2}"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Postgres writes its own log, and kubectl logs shows it like any other."
        },
        {
          "text": "On first start it set up an empty database, restarted itself, and now it's ready to accept connections."
        },
        {
          "text": "Now the question left over from Episode 3: what did the API pods do?"
        },
        {
          "text": "Both are ready, with zero restarts. Nobody touched them: their readiness probe kept asking, and the moment the database answered, they passed."
        },
        {
          "text": "Their logs tell the same story: connected, and the database tables are set up.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "psql",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl exec postgres-0 -n golinks -- psql -U golinks -c '\\dt'",
          "output": [
            "                List of relations",
            " Schema |       Name        | Type  |  Owner",
            "--------+-------------------+-------+---------",
            " public | links             | table | golinks",
            " public | schema_migrations | table | golinks",
            "(2 rows)"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "To look inside, kubectl exec runs psql right in the Postgres pod."
        },
        {
          "text": "There are the tables the API created: links, and a list of the changes it has made to the database."
        },
        {
          "text": "That's as deep as we go into Postgres itself. It's running, it's ready, and its data is on a disk of its own.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "change",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "kubectl apply -f manifests/base/golinks-configmap.yaml",
          "output": [
            "configmap/golinks-config configured"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "command": "kubectl exec deploy/golinks -n golinks -- env | grep LOG_LEVEL",
          "output": [
            "LOG_LEVEL=info"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "command": "kubectl rollout restart deploy/golinks -n golinks",
          "output": [
            "deployment.apps/golinks restarted"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 4,
          "command": "kubectl rollout status deploy/golinks -n golinks",
          "output": [
            "Waiting for deployment \"golinks\" rollout to finish: 1 out of 2 new replicas have been updated...",
            "Waiting for deployment \"golinks\" rollout to finish: 1 old replicas are pending termination...",
            "deployment \"golinks\" successfully rolled out"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "With the pods ready, we can finish what Episode 3 started."
        },
        {
          "text": "In the ConfigMap file, change LOG_LEVEL from info to debug, and apply it."
        },
        {
          "text": "The running pods don't notice. Their environment still says info."
        },
        {
          "text": "So restart them. rollout restart replaces the pods one at a time, just like a new version would roll out."
        },
        {
          "text": "Each new pod has to pass its readiness probe before an old one goes away, so the API is never down.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "debug",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl logs deploy/golinks -n golinks --tail=2",
          "output": [
            "Found 2 pods, using pod/golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-k4xzt",
            "{\"time\":\"2026-11-02T14:31:20Z\",\"level\":\"DEBUG\",\"msg\":\"GET /readyz\",\"status\":200,\"ms\":2}",
            "{\"time\":\"2026-11-02T14:31:25Z\",\"level\":\"DEBUG\",\"msg\":\"GET /readyz\",\"status\":200,\"ms\":1}"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The new pods have new names, and they log at debug level."
        },
        {
          "text": "Every five seconds, there's the readiness probe asking, and getting a 200 back."
        },
        {
          "text": "That's chatty, which is why info is the default. Set it back the same way when you're done.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "next",
      "type": "title",
      "kicker": "Coming up",
      "title": "Episode 5: Reaching it",
      "subtitle": "Services, Ingress and DNS",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "That's the database: a StatefulSet for a stable name, a claim for a disk of its own, and a headless Service so the API can find it."
        },
        {
          "text": "Next time, we put the API where people can reach it, from outside the cluster.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.6
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
